---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site-nav.js';
const path='/about/';
const title='About Malaysian Open Tennis | Independent Malaysian Tennis Resource';
const description='About MalaysianOpenTennis.com, an independent guide to Malaysian tennis events, results, players, rankings, rules and courts by its Editorial Team.';
const updated='5 November 2026';
const schema=[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'AboutPage',name:'About Malaysian Open Tennis',url:new URL(path,SITE.url).href,inLanguage:'en-MY',dateModified:'2026-11-05',publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:SITE.name,url:SITE.url}}];
const crumbs=[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'About',href:path}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema} updated={updated}>
  <div class="page-band"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} /><h1>About Malaysian Open Tennis</h1><p class="intro">An independent guide to tennis in Malaysia: what's on, who won, who to follow, and how the game works.</p></div></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container prose">
    <p class="lead">MalaysianOpenTennis.com is an independent tennis information website for players, fans, parents and coaches in Malaysia. Tennis information here is spread across federation notices, organiser social media, international tour sites and news reports; we bring the useful parts together in one place and link back to where each fact comes from.</p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/tournaments/">Tournament calendar and results</a>: upcoming Malaysian events with entry details, and verified winners from completed events.</li>
      <li><a href="/malaysian-tennis-players/">Malaysian players</a>: a directory and individual profiles with dated rankings and links to official ATP, WTA and ITF pages.</li>
      <li><a href="/news/">News</a>: national team, junior and ITF stories written in our own words with sources.</li>
      <li>Guides to the <a href="/tennis-rules/">rules</a>, <a href="/how-tennis-scoring-works/">scoring</a>, <a href="/tennis-ranking-guide/">rankings</a> and <a href="/malaysia-tennis-events/">entering events</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/tennis-courts-malaysia/">Courts</a>: verified venues with booking contacts, and <a href="/atp-wta-malaysia-history/">the history of ATP and WTA tennis in Malaysia</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>Content is researched, written and maintained by the <strong>{SITE.name} Editorial Team</strong>. We publish under the site's name rather than individual bylines. We are tennis followers and writers, not officials: we do not claim coaching, umpiring or federation credentials, and we do not present our guides as official rulings. For official decisions, rules or entries, use the governing body or organiser linked on each page.</p>

    <h2>How we keep it accurate</h2>
    <p>Every changing fact (a date, a result, a ranking, a price) is checked against an official or primary source and linked on the page where it appears. Rankings and venue details show the date they were checked. When we cannot confirm something, we say so instead of estimating. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains the process in full, including how corrections work.</p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>MalaysianOpenTennis.com is an independent website. It is not the official website of, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by, the ATP, WTA, ITF, Asian Tennis Federation, TennisMalaysia / the Lawn Tennis Association of Malaysia, any tournament organiser, venue, academy or player. Names of events and organisations are used only to identify them. The site carries no sponsored or affiliate content; if that ever changes, it will be clearly labelled and kept separate from editorial pages.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Organisers, clubs, coaches, parents and players are welcome to send event details, results, venue updates or corrections, ideally with a link to a source. See the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
    <div class="related callout info"><strong>More:</strong> <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial policy</a> · <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> · <a href="/tournaments/">Tournaments</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
